---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — nSealr" description="Open-source Nostr signing devices, shared software and explicit development limits.">
  <section class="container page">
    <p class="eyebrow">// about</p>
    <h1 class="page__title">Open-source Nostr signing devices.</h1>
    <p class="lead">nSealr is a non-profit open-source hardware and software project. It develops devices that let a person review and approve what is signed while ordinary clients keep no identity key.</p>
    <h2 class="page__h2">The first milestone</h2>
    <p>A connected ESP32-S3 with display and physical confirmation, without a secure element or persistent identity vault; and independent offline Raspberry Pi and ESP32-P4 signers with session custody. The shared Rust engine, Bridge, CLI/service, browser/client integration and TypeScript SDK belong to the complete user workflow.</p>
    <p>Public-fixture physical signing and verified responses are development evidence. Entropy, recovery, interface lifecycle, installation and each profile's security gates remain explicit. No production-ready device or real-key custody qualification is claimed.</p>
    <h2 class="page__h2">Current owners</h2>
    <ul class="page__list">
      <li><a href="https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr">nsealr</a>: Signer, Bridge, device apps, shared contracts, requirements and the sole task graph.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/nSealr/website">website</a> and <a href="https://github.com/nSealr/.github">.github</a>: public documentation and community guidance.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/nSealr/hardware">hardware</a> and <a href="https://github.com/nSealr/board-sdk">board-sdk</a>: future programmable board and independent embedded platform, outside the initial release path.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Selected companion, raspberry and specs source was consolidated through the reviewed A02 migration. Original repositories preserve source history and licenses. Smartcard research is retired.</p>
    <h2 class="page__h2">Source and contribution</h2>
    <p>Start with the <a href="https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr">current product README</a>, <a href="https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr/tree/main/docs/product">requirements</a> and <a href="/contributing/">contribution guide</a>. Historical capability pages and blog posts are dated context, not a current release catalog.</p>
    <h2 class="page__h2">License</h2>
    <p>Each repository and imported component retains its own license and attribution. Software, specifications and hardware have distinct notices; a migration does not relicense third-party material. See the source LICENSE and retained notices for the artifact you use.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: var(--space-20); max-width: 800px; }
  .page__title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--fg-strong);
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-8);
  }
  .page__h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--fg-strong);
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    margin: var(--space-16) 0 var(--space-6);
  }
  .lead { font-size: var(--text-xl); }
  .page__list { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); padding-left: 1em; }
  .page__repos a { font-family: var(--font-mono); }
</style>
